UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Deduct $20,000 as an offset against ordinary income","Deduct $3,000 currently and carry forward $17,000 as capital loss","Carry back 3 years and forward 5 years as a short-term capital loss","Carry forward indefinitely with no current-year deduction allowed"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 1211(a), corporations may not deduct net capital losses against ordinary income. IRC Section 1212(a) allows corporations to carry net capital losses back 3 years and forward 5 years, treating the carryover as a short-term capital loss regardless of original character.
Wrong (A): Corporations cannot offset capital losses against ordinary income under any circumstances per Section 1211(a).
Wrong (B): The $3,000 individual deduction limit under Section 1211(b) applies only to individuals, not corporations.
