-- Q4820: Alternative Minimum Tax [hard/L3]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["MTC is applied first and the full $15,000 credit can be used this year","General business credits apply first and then the full $15,000 MTC is allowed","General business credits apply first and the MTC is limited to $2,000 remaining","No credits may be used because the TMT nearly equals the regular tax liability"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 53(a), the MTC may offset regular tax only to the extent it exceeds the tentative minimum tax. Per Section 38(c), general business credits are applied first. With $60,000 regular tax and $58,000 TMT, only $2,000 of MTC can be used after applying the $3,000 general business credit.
Wrong (A): The MTC is not applied first; Section 38(c) requires general business credits to be applied before the MTC in the ordering sequence.
Wrong (B): While the ordering is correct, the full $15,000 cannot be used because the MTC is capped at the $2,000 excess of regular tax over TMT.
Wrong (D): Credits can still be used; the $2,000 spread between regular tax and TMT allows partial use of the MTC.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4820;

