-- Q5172: Estate and Gift Tax [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["The $3,000,000 in lifetime gifts reduces the gross estate to a $8,500,000 base","The lifetime gifts are disregarded entirely because no gift tax was actually paid","The adjusted taxable gifts increase the applicable exclusion amount by $3,000,000","The adjusted taxable gifts are added to the taxable estate for tentative tax computation"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 2001(b), the tentative estate tax is calculated on the sum of the taxable estate ($10,500,000) plus adjusted taxable gifts ($3,000,000). The computed tax is then reduced by the gift tax that would have been payable, ensuring cumulative taxation at the highest marginal rate.
Wrong (A): Adjusted taxable gifts do not reduce the gross estate; they are added to the taxable estate in the tentative tax computation.
Wrong (B): Gifts offset by the unified credit are not disregarded; they remain part of the cumulative transfer tax base.
Wrong (C): Adjusted taxable gifts do not increase the exclusion amount; they increase the base on which the tentative tax is calculated.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 5172;

