-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Private benefit applies because it covers outsiders; inurement applies only to insiders","Private inurement applies because any above-market payment violates the prohibition","Neither doctrine applies because the company provides legitimate exempt-purpose services","Both doctrines are identical in scope and apply equally to insiders and outsiders"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Section 501(c)(3), the private benefit doctrine prohibits more than incidental benefits to any private party, whether insider or outsider. Private inurement applies only to insiders with substantial influence. Here, the above-market payment to an unrelated outsider triggers private benefit analysis.
