-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Form W-2, used to report annual employee wages and withholding","Form 1099-MISC, used to report miscellaneous payments to contractors","Form 1099-DIV, used to report dividend distributions to shareholders","Schedule K-1 (Form 1065), used to report each partner''s distributive share"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 6031, a partnership reports each partner''s distributive share of income, deductions, gains, losses, and credits on Schedule K-1 (Form 1065). Each partner uses the K-1 to report those items on their individual return.
Wrong (A): Form W-2 reports wages paid to employees; partners are not employees and receive allocations, not wages.
Wrong (B): Form 1099-MISC reports payments to independent contractors; partnership distributive shares are reported on Schedule K-1.
Wrong (C): Form 1099-DIV reports corporate dividend distributions; partnership income allocations are not dividends.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10758;

-- Q10780: S Corporations [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Northfield may re-elect immediately because it corrected the terminating event","Northfield is permanently barred from re-electing S status after this termination","Northfield may re-elect after three years, starting with the 2028 tax year","Northfield may re-elect for 2030, or earlier with IRS consent under Section 1362(g)"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 1362(g), a corporation whose S election terminates cannot re-elect S status for five tax years without IRS consent. Since the termination occurred during 2024, the first eligible year without consent is the tax year beginning January 1, 2030.
Wrong (A): Correcting the terminating event does not allow immediate re-election; the five-year bar applies regardless when inadvertent termination relief is denied.
Wrong (B): The bar is temporary (five tax years), not permanent; the corporation may re-elect after the waiting period expires.
Wrong (C): The required waiting period is five tax years, not three; a three-year period is not found in Section 1362(g).$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10780;
